==English==

===Etymology===
The "and the following" sense is derived from an abbreviation of {{der|en|la|foliō||on the (next) page}}, ablative of {{m|la|folium||leaf, page}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|grammar}} {{abbr of|en|feminine}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|grammar}} {{abbr of|en|feminine}}
# {{lb|en|biology}} {{abbr of|en|form}} {{non-gloss definition|Used in certain three-part names}}
# {{lb|en|postpositive}} and the following (page, paragraph, etc.)
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Major Trends in Jewish Mysticism|passage=“Alphabet of Rabbi Akiba,” 51. 66. 360 '''f.''', 364 '''f.''', 367|year=1941|author=Gershom Gerhard Scholem|page=445|isbn=0805210423|year_published=1995|chapter=Index|edition=reprint of third revised}}

====Usage notes====
* When used in the sense "and the following", {{m|en||f.}} usually has no space between it and the preceding number and is followed by a period. If more than one following section is meant, {{m|en|ff.}} is used.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|and the following}} {{l|en|et seq.}}

====Related terms====
* {{sense|and the following}} {{l|en|ff.}}

